== 1. Remark 3, two-point example (Theta={w1,w2}, mu uniform, z1=M, z2=-1, y=-1, eta=1/8, Q=delta_w2)
  bound log2/(eta(n+1)) at n=10: 0.5041
  bound log2/(eta(n+1)) at n=100: 0.0549
  bound log2/(eta(n+1)) at n=1000: 0.00554
  M=1e+03 n=1000: loss of progressive mixture of zbar_t = 2.712
  M=1e+06 n=1000: loss of progressive mixture of zbar_t = 2.706e+06
  M=1e3: clip of progressive mixture has loss 4 for every n<=100: True; largest n with loss 4: 399
  lower bound ((M-1)/2-n)/(n+1)>=1 iff n<=(M-3)/4 = 249.25
  loss 4 exceeds the bound exactly for n in [1, 100] within 0..100
  M=10, T=1: zbar_0=4.5, (zbar_0-y)^2=30.25, (clip zbar_0-y)^2=4, -(1/eta)log(Z1/Z0)=1.7526

== 2. Prop C.3(c): root of 4u+sqrt(2u)=1/4
  v=(sqrt6-sqrt2)/8=0.129410: 4v^2+sqrt2 v=0.250000; v^2=0.016747; (2-sqrt3)/16=0.016747
  brute force min sigma^2 k over the feasible set (sigma^2<=1): 0.016765
  sigma=2.0: k=1/(16 sigma^4): sigma^2 sqrt(2k)=0.3536, eta sigma^2 n/m_nu=0.01562
  sigma=10.0: k=1/(16 sigma^4): sigma^2 sqrt(2k)=0.3536, eta sigma^2 n/m_nu=0.00063
  record: eta n < 0.01675 => |fhat| <= e^(4 eta n)-1 = 0.0693, excess >= 0.8662

